  "scope": "Exact source rollback selection uses captured initial actual_roots while physical callback outcomes thread current progress. Symbolic recurrence covers all sixteen partitions without unrolling. Explicit ForwardPartitionFrames callback contract preserves later partition observations after successful earlier rollback and is the necessary native NOMT/locking/observation interface for reusing original changing-root recovery; it never forces own-root restoration, success, healthy state or durability. Eight reports (four program/contract definitions, four proofs) establish recurrence equivalence under frames/tail correspondence, failing callback progress/suffix suppression, source prepare and full recovery equality under explicit native frames. Original recovery reports reused once without replay. Independently observed physical root/poison semantics, actual final root read, native partition representation/session isolation/locks, serde/file IO, ownership and source execution correspondence remain interfaces. Zero native/control/full certification. All eight declarations retain full original type/axiom reports. Whole 01 compiler failure and 03 unused-simp warning earn zero credit; prepared 02 never executed. Only induction/final equality tactics repaired; definitions/contracts and native forward-frame premise unchanged. Rejected object retained unused, no object bytes. Native frames/observations/ownership/IO/library/OS interfaces remain explicit. Zero native/control/full certification credit.",
